From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:54:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: the MT7986's firmware commands
 (mt7915/mcu.c)

151 KUnit tests in 9 suites, run against the fake firmware: every
command the driver builds for the MT7986, checked field by field. They
also cover the replies and events it parses, and the error paths. In-scope
coverage of mt7915/mcu.c goes from 1.2% to 96.2% of lines (1934/2010),
and all 108 of its functions.

- mt7915-mcu, -mcu-bss, -mcu-sta, -mcu-rate: station and BSS records.
  - STA_REC and BSS_INFO TLV order and contents, and WTBL.
  - HE/VHT/HT capabilities and beamforming records.
  - Rate control, fixed rates and SMPS.
  - Block ack, MUAR, beacons and in-band discovery.
  - TWT, BSS color, protection and spatial reuse.
- mt7915-mcu-fw, -fw-events, -fw-chan, -fw-power, -fw-misc: everything else.
  - Firmware bring-up and shutdown, and the message transport (TXD).
  - Timeouts and recovery.
  - Unsolicited events.
  - Channel info and calibration (DPD, group cal), background radar and
    DFS thresholds.
  - Tx power and SKU tables, and thermal.
  - EEPROM, EDCA, RED, VOW, rx airtime, MU/RU stats and rx rate.

Six tests are skipped. Each one shows a suspected driver bug, kept so it
can be fixed and then un-skipped:
- Setting a station's tx power back to automatic (0) gives -EINVAL on
  multi-chain radios: mt76_get_power_bound() subtracts the chain gain.
- 160 MHz channels never use the MT7986's BW160 DPD slots.
- get_eeprom/get_eeprom_free_block read past a short reply.
- muru_debug_get reads past a short reply.
- At 160 MHz with implicit beamforming, ibf_nrow = 1 is overwritten by
  tx_ant.
- With implicit beamforming on, HE-only stations get an all-zero
  STA_REC_BF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
